30,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The minutes show a total lack of review for years. This stagnation is exactly how resentment builds up silently.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,I found out that some people are actually willing to pay more for a spot! That's so surprising and helpful!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The morning rush is a shoving match. People are moving other bikes just to get out, which leads to damage and frustration.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"As expected, the ledger is bare. We have no dedicated fund for this, and the current cash collection is a tedious, low-yield mess.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The handover file confirms it. The administrative burden is already high for very little return. Adding complex billing will be a nightmare.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, that shoving match is a symptom of a system that ignores human behavior. We cannot let a new rule exacerbate this.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"But if people are willing to pay, maybe we can use that money to improve the parking area? That would be a win-win!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, money won't fix a layout where bikes are packed too tightly. The physical friction is the primary issue, not the funding.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, you're too focused on the ""shoving."" If we implement a paid system, we can afford better frames or a professional manager.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, a professional manager costs more than the small fees we'd collect. We'd just be creating more paperwork for the treasurer.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"I'm concerned that a ""paid"" system will create a class divide in the building. Those who can't pay will feel marginalized.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"I don't want anyone to feel left out! But I also don't want the ""grumbling"" to continue. Maybe a lottery is fairer?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,A lottery doesn't solve the physical congestion. We need a system that accounts for how often and when bikes are actually used.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"A lottery is a lazy man's solution. It's fair in a vacuum, but it's fiscally useless. We should monetize the demand.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,A lottery is the lowest maintenance option. Any system involving payments or usage tracking requires a dedicated administrator who will eventually quit.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"We must prioritize social harmony. A system that feels ""unfair"" or ""elitist"" will destroy the atmosphere in the lobby.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I just want everyone to be happy. If we can find a way to be fair without making people feel bad, that's the best!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"We need to be realistic. If we don't address the physical congestion, the ""atmosphere"" will be ruined by people arguing over scratched paint.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,Let's stop the sentimentality. We have a resource shortage. The most rational way to allocate a scarce resource is through a price mechanism.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"I'll support whatever requires the least amount of monthly oversight. I've seen too many ""great ideas"" collapse because the workload was too high.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
