58,3,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A is a disaster for social cohesion. It turns neighbors into competitors. Option C is too chaotic and will lead to more fighting.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,Option C sounds a bit scary because of the shoving Ryuji mentioned. But Option B feels very fair because everyone has the same chance!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C is exactly what we have now, just with different racks. It doesn't solve the shoving match. Option B provides stability for a year.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option B is a waste of potential revenue. Option A is the only one that treats the parking space as the asset it actually is.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A requires monthly billing and collection. Option C requires constant physical policing. Option B is a once-a-year event.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, I agree that Option B is the most stable. It's a random act of fate, which is easier to accept than a financial or physical battle.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Shunichi, is the money really more important than the neighbors getting along? I think a lottery would make people feel it's a fair game!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, while B is stable, it doesn't account for the rain exposure I found. Some people will get ""bad"" spots and feel cheated for a whole year.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Yumi, it's not about ""importance,"" it's about efficiency. Why give away for free something that people are explicitly willing to pay for?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, the ""bad spots"" are a minor grievance compared to the administrative collapse of a payment system. B is the only sustainable choice.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"Even if some spots are less desirable, the lottery is a transparent process. It prevents the ""stagnation"" I saw in the minutes.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"I'm worried about the rain spots too, but maybe we can just be kind to each other? I'll vote for the lottery to keep the peace!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"If we go with B, we must at least acknowledge the quality difference of the spots. But compared to the current chaos, it is an improvement.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"You're all choosing the path of least resistance. It's a shame. However, if the alternative is a total lack of funding, A is still superior.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"The ""path of least resistance"" is the only path that doesn't end in a vacant treasurer's seat and a pile of unpaid invoices.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I will vote for Option B. It is the most logically stable outcome for the social dynamics of this building.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm voting for Option B too! Let's make it a fun event every year and keep everyone smiling!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I'll vote for Option B. It provides a fixed order for a set period, which will stop the daily shoving matches and the uncertainty.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'll vote for Option A. I cannot in good conscience support a system that ignores the financial reality of the building's assets.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I vote for Option B. It minimizes the administrative burden and prevents the cycle of management failure we've seen in the past.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
